  <section class="seo-intro" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2 class="h-sec">Traditional wisdom, <span class="it" style="color:var(--teal)">simple ritual.</span></h2>
    <p>Ashwagandha is one of Ayurveda’s best-known botanicals. Its root has been taken for centuries as a <i>rasayana</i> — a herb traditionally used to support vitality — often stirred into warm milk at the end of the day.</p><p>Veda Apothecary Ashwagandha Powder is made from the root alone, with no additives, fillers or preservatives. Whisk it into golden moon milk, warm water or a smoothie as an unhurried evening ritual.</p>
    <h3 class="h-sub">How to build the ritual</h3>
    <ol class="steps-list"><li><b>Wind down.</b> Warm milk, a pinch of cinnamon and a teaspoon of Ashwagandha make a cozy end to the day.</li><li><b>Balance the taste.</b> Honey, cardamom and nutmeg round out Ashwagandha’s earthy flavor.</li><li><b>Check first.</b> Ashwagandha may not be suitable during pregnancy or alongside some medications — consult a healthcare professional.</li></ol>
    <p class="disc-inline"><b>*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</b> Consult a healthcare professional before use, especially if you are pregnant, nursing, or taking medication.</p>
